    "text": "Portugal pledges 'full support' for Pakistan's GSP+ status! 🇵🇰🇵🇹\nAccording to Dawn, Portuguese Foreign Minister Paulo Rangel said on Monday that Pakistan has Portugal's full support for the European Union's GSP+ status, during delegation-level talks in Islamabad with Deputy Prime Minister and Foreign Minister Ishaq Dar. The two ministers agreed to set up a Pakistan-Portugal Joint Ministerial Commission to boost trade and investment. Pakistan's current GSP+ status runs until 2027, and Rangel said this was the first visit to Pakistan by a Portuguese delegation in 19 years.\nWill stronger ties with Europe help Pakistani exports grow? Tell us below 👇\n\nImage: AI-generated illustration.\n\n#RiseUpPakistan #PakistanPortugal #GSPPlus #Trade #PakistanNews",
